WEBVTT

00:06:27.716 --> 00:06:30.316
almost all of us
want to do the right thing.

00:06:30.356 --> 00:06:33.156
At some level, these moral regrets
are very heartening.

00:06:33.196 --> 00:06:36.476
The idea that people are bugged
for years, decades,

00:06:36.476 --> 00:06:39.676
by these moral breaches
earlier in their life.

00:06:39.676 --> 00:06:41.876
I think most of us
want to do the right thing.

00:06:41.876 --> 00:06:43.316
And then connection regrets.

00:06:43.916 --> 00:06:46.516
We want love, not love only
in the romantic sense,

00:06:46.556 --> 00:06:49.796
but love in the broader sense
of connection and relationship

00:06:49.796 --> 00:06:51.476
and affinity with other people.

00:06:51.516 --> 00:06:53.596
And so in a weird way,

00:06:53.596 --> 00:06:58.916
this negative emotion of regret
points the way to a good life.

00:06:58.916 --> 00:07:01.956
By studying regret, we know
what constitutes a good life,